## Caveats

* 'COMPILED' here means the .s assembled via 'as --64' — it does not mean the program runs correctly. Many x86_*.oo fixtures are designed around the hardcoded Float/List templates; the assembly assembles but the runtime output is wrong for any source the templates don't recognize.
* 'REFUSED' means the emit printed 'ERR x86_emit ...' and exited non-zero.
* 'ASM-FAIL' means the .s was produced but GNU as could not assemble it (e.g. x86-ssa path emits pseudo-ops that conflict).
* This is a COMPILE-only probe. There is no RUN probe — many of the 'COMPILED' outputs will produce wrong output at runtime (silent miscompile).

## Per-fixture details
Full per-fixture results in /tmp/x86probe/x86.txt and /tmp/x86probe/ssa.txt (tsv: name<TAB>result)

## Methodology

For each fixture in ooda/fixtures/*.oo:
  1. Run ./oodac/oodac emit-x86 <f> 2>&1 — capture stdout+stderr
  2. If output starts with 'ERR', mark REFUSED
  3. If output contains '_start', 'main:', or '.text', write to /tmp/x86probe/results/<bn>.x86.s
  4. Run 'as --64 -o <bn>.o <bn>.s'. Success → COMPILED. Failure → ASM-FAIL.
  5. Repeat for emit-x86-ssa.
No run probe; no output-correctness check. This is a coarse filter.
